.* NETPRB: the task menu for network problems.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='NETPRB'.
:IMPORT NAME=WRKPRB PNLGRP=QHSXCMD.
:KEYL NAME=MENUKEYS HELP='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F13 ACTION='MENU INFO'.F13=Information Assistant
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='MENU MAIN'.F16=System Main menu
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=NETPRB HELP=HLPNETPRB KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.Network Problem Handling
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD WRKPRB' HELP=WRKPRB.Work with problems
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='CMD ?WRKALR' HELP='NETPRB/OPT2'.Work with alerts
:MENUI OPTION=3 ACTION='CMD ?VFYCMN' HELP='NETPRB/OPT3'.Verify communications
:MENUI OPTION=4 ACTION='MENU NETWORK' HELP='NETPRB/OPT4'.Network management
:MENUI OPTION=5 ACTION='MENU FILETFR' HELP='NETPRB/OPT5'.Send or receive files
:MENUI OPTION=6 ACTION='CMD ?STRPASTHR' HELP='NETPRB/OPT6'.Access a remote system
:MENUI OPTION=7 ACTION='CMD ?WRKALRD' HELP='NETPRB/OPT7'.Work with alert descriptions
:MENUI OPTION=8 ACTION='CMD ?VFYAPPCCNN' HELP='NETPRB/OPT8'.Verify APPC connection
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPNETPRB.Network Problem Handling - Help
:P.The problems this system logged and the tools for network problems.
Alerts, APPC and pass-through are not in this release; their options say
so.
:P.Type an option number or a command and press Enter. F4 prompts the
command, F9 brings the previous one back, F12 returns to the menu shown
before this one.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F13=Information Assistant
:PD.Shows menu INFO.
:PT.F16=System Main menu
:PD.Shows menu MAIN.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='NETPRB/OPT2'.Work with alerts
:P.Option 2. Runs the WRKALR command&colon. Work with alerts.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='NETPRB/OPT3'.Verify communications
:P.Option 3. Runs the VFYCMN command&colon. Verify communications.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='NETPRB/OPT4'.Network management
:P.Option 4. Shows menu NETWORK&colon. Network management.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='NETPRB/OPT5'.Send or receive files
:P.Option 5. Shows menu FILETFR&colon. Send or receive files.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='NETPRB/OPT6'.Access a remote system
:P.Option 6. Runs the STRPASTHR command&colon. Access a remote system.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='NETPRB/OPT7'.Work with alert descriptions
:P.Option 7. Runs the WRKALRD command&colon. Work with alert
descriptions.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='NETPRB/OPT8'.Verify APPC connection
:P.Option 8. Runs the VFYAPPCCNN command&colon. Verify APPC connection.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
